      "html": "<p>It is a criminal offence for a driver or operator to use an unroadworthy vehicle on the road (DVSA guide). Operator licence holders must keep vehicles fit and safe.</p><p>The DVSA Guide to Maintaining Roadworthiness says a walkaround check must be done every day a vehicle is used, before it goes out. The driver reports defects. The operator makes sure the vehicle is safe and keeps the records.</p><p>The Traffic Commissioner looks at your record. Missed checks, defects driven on and gaps in the records all count against you.</p>"
