      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>Is a daily walkaround check a legal requirement for UK operators?</h3><p>Yes. The DVSA guide says a walkaround check must be done every day a vehicle is used, and it is a criminal offence for a driver or operator to use an unroadworthy vehicle on the road. Poor records count against you when the Traffic Commissioner reviews the licence.</p><h3>How long must walkaround check records be kept?</h3><p>At least 15 months. Keep them easy to reach for management and enforcement. Electronic records are fine if they cannot be changed afterwards.</p><h3>What happens if a defect is found during the walkaround check?</h3><p>Report it at once to the operator or transport manager. If it is a safety defect, such as brakes, steering or tyres, the vehicle must not be used on the road until it is repaired. The driver records the defect. The operator records the fix and the date.</p><h3>Can walkaround checks be completed electronically?</h3><p>Yes, if the record cannot be changed afterwards and is kept for the full period. A WhatsApp check with a timed PDF record can do this.</p>"
